Today's game ends.
I am very tired, but I am very happy.
I go to the reception desk.
I give the rented racket back to the man there.
"Thank you, Dada," I say.
"I will come back next Thursday."
The man keeps the racket.
"Madam, come again next week," he says with a smile.
"Yes, definitely."
"I come here to play every Thursday now," I say.
I step out of the club.
There is a nice cool breeze outside.
I walk towards the bus stop.
Now I have new friends in Mumbai.
Amit, Neha, and Sanjay are very nice people.
I like to play with them.
My new Thursday routine is very nice.
I go home happily.
